For the fixed analytic data of [thm:interpolation](#thm:interpolation) there is a polynomial $M(D)$ with the following property. Let $W$ be an irreducible affine variety of degree at most $D$ on which $a$ is nonconstant. On a branch above the generic point of a component of $V_W(a)$, every allowed expression $E$ which is not identically zero satisfies $$\label{eq:divisorial-zero-estimate}
 \operatorname{ord}_{\mathfrak p}E
 <M(D)\operatorname{ord}_{\mathfrak p}a.$$ The bound is independent of the heights of the coefficients of $W$ and of the expression.

Let $W$ be an irreducible affine variety of dimension $k\geq1$ with coordinate $a$ nonconstant, let $f$ be regular on $W$, and let $m\ge1$ be an integer. Suppose $$\operatorname{ord}_{\mathfrak p}f
 <m\operatorname{ord}_{\mathfrak p}a$$ on every normalization branch over the generic components of $V_W(a)$. Let $W'$ be the affine graph closure of $q=f/a^m$ over $W\setminus V(a)$. For every regular function $g$ on $W$, $$\label{eq:graph-fiber-dimension}
 \dim V\bigl(I(W'),a,q+g\bigr)\leq k-2.$$ The set is empty when $k=1$; the same convention applies if $V_W(a)$ is empty.

Choose the vectors of [prop:small-vectors](#prop:small-vectors). Their affine coordinates in the fixed frame satisfy $$\label{eq:dr-global}
 \mathrm h\!\left(z(t),a,P\right)\le C(h+\log d).$$ There are center neighborhoods at every place, with a single integral description outside a fixed finite set of rational primes, such that for any selected weighted set $\mathcal V$ on the actual center branches, $$\label{eq:dr-local}
 \sum_{v\in\mathcal V}w_v
       \log\max(1,\left\lVert z(t),P\right\rVert_v)
       \le C(1+\log h+\log d).$$ These statements hold for the finitely many conjugate fixed charts. They also hold after a bounded denominator and a polarized isogeny of any one fixed multiplier are applied to the vectors.

Use the fixed center disks of [prop:dr-size](#prop:dr-size), [prop:good-comparison](#prop:good-comparison), and at every remaining prime impose <a href="#eq:factorial-disk" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:factorial-disk">[eq:factorial-disk]</a>. Let $\mathcal V_0(t)$ be all weighted embeddings at which $t$ belongs to these actual branches. Then $$\label{eq:proximity-sum}
 \sum_{v\in\mathcal V_0(t)}w_v\log(1/|a|_v)
       \ge c h-C\bigl(1+\log^2(dh)\bigr).$$ In particular the sum is at least $c h/2$ if $h\ge Q_0(d)$ for a fixed polynomial $Q_0$.
